From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wgl: ChoosePixelFormat picks only a format SetPixelFormat
 takes

stw_pixelformat_choose looked through the extended formats too (the 16-
and 32-bit-float ones meant for wglChoosePixelFormatARB), which
DescribePixelFormat doesn't list and DrvSetPixelFormat refuses. A game
asking for a 16-bit pixel format (Alone in the Dark: The New Nightmare)
was given B5G6R5, its SetPixelFormat failed, and wglCreateContext had no
pixel format to make a context with: every GL call then had no context
and the game closed. It now chooses among the listed formats, as a
Windows driver does, so the game gets the closest 32-bit one. A choice
that was already a listed format is the same as before.
---
 src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_pixelformat.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_pixelformat.c b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_pixelformat.c
index 5b42ba0..681bfe8 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_pixelformat.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_pixelformat.c
@@ -495,7 +495,10 @@ stw_pixelformat_choose(HDC hdc, CONST PIXELFORMATDESCRIPTOR *ppfd)
    uint bestindex;
    uint bestdelta;
 
-   count = stw_pixelformat_get_extended_count(hdc);
+   /* Only the formats DescribePixelFormat lists, which are all SetPixelFormat takes: a request
+    * for a 16-bit format matched an extended one (B5G6R5), which SetPixelFormat then refused, so
+    * the program got no context at all. The extended formats are for wglChoosePixelFormatARB. */
+   count = stw_pixelformat_get_count(hdc);
    bestindex = 0;
    bestdelta = ~0U;
 
